<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kufra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kufra oases</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kufra is a group of oases in the Libyan Desert of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>. In 1895 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senussi-order">Senussi order</a> moved its headquarters there, making it a hub of the caravan trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a>. Italian forces captured it in 1931, and Free French troops under Leclerc took it from the Italians in 1941.</p></div>
